{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgszdrhtUAGRAS33Dr8YH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MLQT7G6mch5iHhAk3C2zud","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"printf 'node_modules/\\n' > .gitignore && cat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Answer\n\n## What was done\n\n- Added the Hedera JavaScript SDK at the current npm version, pinned exactly: `@hashgraph/sdk@2.81.0` (`npm view @hashgraph/sdk version`). `package-lock.json` was generated by `npm install`.\n- Added `src/transfer.ts`, run with `npx tsx src/transfer.ts`. It:\n  - reads `OPERATOR_ID`, `OPERATOR_KEY` (DER-encoded ED25519 private key, hex), `RECIPIENT_ID` and `VALID_START` (Unix seconds) from the environment (loaded from `.env` via `dotenv`);\n  - builds a `TransferTransaction` moving 1 hbar from the operator to the recipient, memo `invoice 42`, node account `0.0.3`, transaction ID `OPERATOR_ID@VALID_START`;\n  - freezes it locally, signs it with the operator key, and prints only the signed transaction bytes as hex.\n- No network calls are made: the transaction is frozen with an explicit node and transaction ID, so no client or node lookup is needed.\n- Added `.gitignore` containing `node_modules/` so installed dependencies are not picked up by git.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with no errors.\n- `npx tsx src/transfer.ts` runs and prints a hex string.\n- Decoding that output offline with the SDK (`Transaction.fromBytes`) gives:\n  - memo: `invoice 42`\n  - transaction ID: `0.0.1001@1793000000.000000000`\n  - node: `0.0.3`\n  - transfers: `0.0.1001 = -1 ℏ`, `0.0.1002 = +1 ℏ`\n  - one signature present\n\n## Choices made\n\n- The SDK version is pinned exactly (no `^`), so the transaction format does not change under future installs.\n- `VALID_START` is parsed as a Unix timestamp in seconds; non-integer or negative values abort with an error.\n- The script aborts with a clear message if any required environment variable is missing.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `.env` is tracked in git and contains an `OPERATOR_KEY` value. Even though the values are test values, committing private keys is risky; consider moving `.env` into `.gitignore` and rotating any real key that has been committed. I did not change this.\n- `README.md` says a separate service submits the transactions. This script does not submit anything, which matches that design.\nEOF\nnpx tsc --noEmit && echo TSC_OK; git status --short","description":"Write ANSWER.md and recheck typecheck and git status"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":497,"cache_read_input_tokens":27032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":497},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75fbdad7-b23a-49b0-b6c6-b73211db086d","uuid":"89044ec8-fd1c-4262-8c39-097bd4db7fa4","timestamp":"2026-11-09T20:35:30.247Z","request_id":"req_011CgszdrPY2YFSr29oQyNiw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MLQT7G6mch5iHhAk3C2zud":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-NQDaA6 && printf 'node_modules/\\n' > .gitignore && cat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Answer\n\n## What was done\n\n- Added the Hedera JavaScript SDK at the current npm version, pinned exactly: `@hashgraph/sdk@2.81.0` (`npm view @hashgraph/sdk version`). `package-lock.json` was generated by `npm install`.\n- Added `src/transfer.ts`, run with `npx tsx src/transfer.ts`. It:\n  - reads `OPERATOR_ID`, `OPERATOR_KEY` (DER-encoded ED25519 private key, hex), `RECIPIENT_ID` and `VALID_START` (Unix seconds) from the environment (loaded from `.env` via `dotenv`);\n  - builds a `TransferTransaction` moving 1 hbar from the operator to the recipient, memo `invoice 42`, node account `0.0.3`, transaction ID `OPERATOR_ID@VALID_START`;\n  - freezes 